\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Attainable outcome--cost set}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{multi-objective}

\p{Fix evaluator utilities #{u_1,\ldots,u_m}. Let
#{\mathbf J(P)\in\mathbb R^m} collect their expected performances for the
random policy returned by #{P}. The \strong{attainable outcome--cost set} is}

##{
 \mathfrak A(M_0)
 =\left\{(\mathbf J(P),\mathbb E[C(P)]):
   P\in\mathfrak P(M_0),\ \operatorname{Trust}(P)\right\}.
}

\p{This is an FTIP proposal. Section 4.7.4 of
\citef{boyd2004convex} motivates representing a multi-objective problem by
its feasible objective vectors. FTIP adds lifecycle costs and the trust
predicate.}

\p{The set records what was reached before choosing an order on outcomes.
Scalar, Pareto, and worst-group summaries below answer different questions
about this same set.}
